A. John Kennedy
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
Intelligence Officer, Narcotics Control Bureau \(NCB\), Madurai Sub Zone
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act 1985

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
NDPS Act Section 8\(c\), NDPS Act Section 20\(b\)\(ii\)\(C\), NDPS Act Section 37

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
NDPS Bail, Commercial Quantity, Section 37 NDPS, Twin Conditions, Reasonable Grounds

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Petitioner was apprehended with 42 kg of Ganja \(commercial quantity\). Petitioner moved second regular bail application alleging procedural non-compliance with Section 50 NDPS Act.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Whether non-compliance with Section 50 can be decided at bail stage when search was of vehicle and luggage?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Section 37 NDPS mandates satisfaction that accused is not guilty and unlikely to commit offense while on bail.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Section 50 NDPS Act applies only to personal search of the accused, not vehicle search. Twin conditions under Section 37 bar bail in commercial quantity seizure.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Bail Application Dismissed; Commercial quantity recovery bars bail under Section 37 of NDPS Act.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice G. Ilangovan
Madras High Court \(Madurai Bench\)
